@template.layout(
    title = "About LifeVerdict",
    description = "LifeVerdict is an inspection ask pre-send check for buyer agents and buyers under contract.",
    content = @`
        <div class="support-shell">
            <section class="support-hero">
                <div class="section-kicker">About the product</div>
                <h1 class="support-title">LifeVerdict is built for the buyer agent inside the inspection response window.</h1>
                <p class="support-lede">
                    LifeVerdict helps a buyer agent turn inspection findings into a seller-credit ask, fallback posture, and sendable negotiation packet, with buyers under contract as the secondary direct user.
                </p>
                <div class="support-meta">
                    <span>Buyer-agent workflow first</span>
                    <span>Tool-first product</span>
                    <span>Updated April 23, 2026</span>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="support-grid">
                <article class="support-card">
                    <h2>Primary customer</h2>
                    <ul class="support-list">
                        <li>Buyer agents who need to compress the inspection report into one clear ask.</li>
                        <li>Small buyer-agent teams handling repeated inspection-response workflows.</li>
                        <li>Deals where timing, evidence, and wording matter as much as the number.</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>

                <article class="support-card">
                    <h2>Secondary customer</h2>
                    <ul class="support-list">
                        <li>Buyers under contract who want a stronger first draft before talking with their agent.</li>
                        <li>Buyers who need help separating true leverage from report noise.</li>
                        <li>Users who still expect the result to be agent-ready rather than DIY advice.</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>

                <article class="support-card">
                    <h2>Who it is not for</h2>
                    <ul class="support-list">
                        <li>Not an inspector report-writing suite.</li>
                        <li>Not a lender or insurer workflow product in the current surface.</li>
                        <li>Not a generic renovation budgeting site or contractor lead marketplace.</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
            </section>

            <section class="support-grid mt-5">
                <article class="support-card">
                    <h2>What it does</h2>
                    <ul class="support-list">
                        <li>Separates lead negotiation items from verify-later items and cosmetic noise.</li>
                        <li>Scopes the opening ask to what belongs in this response window.</li>
                        <li>Produces agent-ready copy, fallback posture, and evidence checklist.</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>

                <article class="support-card">
                    <h2>Why the customer is narrow</h2>
                    <p>
                        Repeated value comes from buyer-side deal flow, not from broad homeowner traffic. The product is strongest when someone needs to turn an inspection report into a message and a number before the response window closes.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article class="support-card">
                    <h2>What success looks like</h2>
                    <p>
                        A buyer agent reuses the tool across multiple live deals, and a buyer under contract can still use it directly without turning the product into a broad education site.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </section>

            <section class="support-grid mt-5">
                <article class="support-card">
                    <h2>Why we built it</h2>
                    <p>
                        Most buyer agents do not need another long explanation after the inspection. They need a way to check whether the proposed ask is defensible before it reaches the listing side. LifeVerdict compresses report language, evidence, and pricing context into one reviewed packet.
                    </p>
                    <div class="support-callout">
                        <strong>The core job</strong>
                        Reduce inspection anxiety into a defensible next message.
                    </div>
                </article>

                <article class="support-card">
                    <h2>How validation works</h2>
                    <p>
                        Copying, printing, and marking the packet useful remain free while the product is being validated in real deal flow. The product is judged by whether the packet earns repeated use when an inspection response is actually due.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article class="support-card">
                    <h2>Operating principle</h2>
                    <p>
                        The product should feel like a transaction desk. Every screen should help the user decide what to ask for, why it belongs in scope, and what they can send next.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </section>
        </div>
    `
)
